  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_loop_reachability.py.archive
  native_format graf
  known_gap unlockable (not yet reachable) opportunities are refused; auto-executing their unlocks is the next step
  known_gap every source this entry names is archived, so nothing here is a live implementation a reader can open and run. Whether a native owner has taken this work over is not established in this entry; until one is named and witnessed here, the architecture stands on retired code.
architecture collapse-front
  canonical_name CollapseFront
  owns SupportStructure
  derived SupportStructure
  consumes Actor
  consumes Relation
  publishes SupportStructure
  family opportunity
  domain Opportunity / Provenance Structure
  layer opportunity
  semantic_question If this fact is withdrawn, which conclusions lose all support -- and which single facts is a given conclusion load-bearing on?
  purpose The retraction dual of reachability. UnlockGraph computes what is reachable forward; CollapseFront computes the inverse over a monotone AND/OR support lattice: collapse_front(fact) = conclusions that go dark if that fact alone is retracted; critical_support(conclusion) = the facts whose solo retraction collapses it. The two are exact transposes of one boolean collapse matrix. This makes the constitution's no-maturity-laundering rule a runtime query: retract a witness and CollapseFront names every claim that had no independent support.
  maturity measured
  node_types Ground
  node_types Conclusion
  edge_types supported_by
  edge_types collapses
  internal_calculus monotone AND/OR support fixpoint; single-retraction propagation over the collapse matrix
  invariant collapse_front and critical_support are exact transposes of one boolean matrix M[conclusion][ground]
  invariant support is monotone (support only, no negation): adding a fact never removes a conclusion, so the fixpoint is order-independent
  invariant a conclusion survives losing any single ground iff it has at least two independent supports
  forbidden_inference collapses under retraction -> the conclusion was false (it means no surviving independent support, not incorrectness)
  forbidden_inference single-retraction collapse -> that fact is the sole cause (co-critical grounds may each be independently solo-critical)
  forbidden_inference absent from every collapse front -> the conclusion is true (robust support is not truth; it may also be already unsupported)
  interacts actor-graph
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/support_lattice.py.archive
  source_path cmd/BonfyreAtlas/src/main.c
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_support_lattice.py.archive
  witness bun test architecture/tests/atlas_collapse.test.mjs proves solo retraction, robust support and external-vs-missing witness classification
  source_lineage retraction dual harvested from run6/run7 DBSP retraction algebra
  known_gap actor-graph CollapseFront was measured on 68 actors (org:tarbell-center load-bearing for 279 of 338 conclusions); this Bun Atlas self-audit covers only the OR-over-witness maturity specialization. Extending grounds to occurrences/evidence witnesses and maintaining the full collapse matrix incrementally in DBSP remains open

architecture fortification-plan
  canonical_name FortificationPlan
  owns FortificationPlan
  derived FortificationPlan
  consumes SupportStructure
  consumes Actor
  consumes Corroboration
  publishes FortificationPlan
  family opportunity
  domain Opportunity / Institutional Capacity
  layer opportunity
  semantic_question Which single real-world action most increases robust reachable capacity right now?
  purpose Composes CollapseFront with reachability into ranked action over the real relationship graph. VERIFY: an asserted actor many live conclusions rest on (leverage = its CollapseFront) -- confirm the assumption before acting on it. DIVERSIFY: a high-value conclusion (funding/authority/opportunity) standing on a single actor -- add a second independent path. Emits the next moves ranked by leverage and publishes the plan into the live fabric, so the loop and a human read the priorities BonfyreFS serves. Not an audit; an action list.
  maturity implemented
  # Demoted: every witness this carried was archived. The evidence was
  # retired and the claim was never revisited, which is the laundering the
  # atlas forbids -- reclaiming measured needs a witness that runs today.
  known_gap fortification-plan lost its live witness to archival and holds implemented until one runs again
  node_types Action
  edge_types prioritizes
  state_types verify
  state_types diversify
  internal_calculus leverage rank over the CollapseFront collapse matrix, split by actor confidence
  invariant a verified actor is never a verification target; leverage counts only value-bearing conclusions
  invariant the plan ranks moves, never executes them; reachability stops at the human/external commit line
  forbidden_inference high leverage -> the action is authorized or free
  forbidden_inference fragile support -> the relationship is false (fragility is structural, not truth)
  forbidden_inference published plan -> the action was taken
  interacts collapse-front
  interacts actor-graph
  interacts unlock-graph
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/fortification.py.archive
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_fortification.py.archive
  source_lineage CollapseFront applied to real institutional prioritization
  known_gap measured on the live 68-actor graph: Tarbell Center is the top verify target (279 live conclusions rest on an only-asserted actor), then the funder set at 15 each; plan published to the live fabric as fortification-plan.v1. Feeding the leverage signal back into reachable_capacity so the loop pursues fragile-but-reachable capacity before it collapses is the next step

architecture resource-activation
  canonical_name ResourceActivationGraph
  owns ResourceActivation
  consumes Authority
  consumes ProviderState
  publishes ResourceActivation
  family opportunity
  domain Opportunity / Resource
  layer opportunity
  semantic_question How does a currently-unavailable resource become reachable and usable?
  purpose World-expansion: capability gap -> candidate -> qualification -> eligibility -> authority -> activation mechanism (service lease, GPU, human commitment, voucher, credential). Only after activation does ProviderGraph see a usable resource.
  maturity implemented
  node_types CapabilityGap
  node_types ResourceCandidate
  node_types ActivationMechanism
  edge_types qualifies
  edge_types activates
  state_types gap
  state_types candidate
  state_types qualified
  state_types eligible
  state_types authorized
  state_types activated
  internal_calculus ordered activation state machine, authority-gated
  invariant only a resource at activated is usable; available is not activated
  invariant activate authority is never short-circuited by qualification or binding
  invariant actor/mechanism selection is an independent fact: selection_detail is separate from DemandBook eligibility provenance and a refresh or retraction of SupplyMatch may not erase the selection
  invariant reconciliation reads the current AuthorityGraph activate grant and current ServiceLifecycle binding and writes neither; losing eligibility, authority or binding immediately lowers the derived state
  forbidden_inference provider available -> resource activation bypassed
  forbidden_inference resource eligible -> resource authorized
  forbidden_inference actor selected -> activate authority, service binding or activation
  native_format graf
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/resource_activation.py.archive
  source_path engine/core/src/activation.c
  source_path engine/core/include/bf_activation.h
  source_path engine/core/src/service_lifecycle.c
  source_path engine/core/include/bf_service_lifecycle.h
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/src/main.c
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_resource_activation.py.archive
  witness engine/core/tests/activation_test.c
  witness engine/core/tests/service_lifecycle_test.c
  witness components/BonfyreProject/tests/activation_projection_test.sh
  source_lineage SEED-A recursive organ document
  known_gap no standing policy elects a provider/actor, mints activate authority or creates a binding; those remain explicit institutional facts, so eligibility can accumulate without activation and that is the intended membrane
